00:15:19,500 --> 00:15:21,980
view- Remember Peyton Powell talked about that.

240
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:25,500
to keep the main aim and view, Can this scout

241
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:28,300
exercise the kind of integrity to evaluate

242
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:31,740
himself fairly. Is he weaving these concepts

243
00:15:31,740 --> 00:15:35,100
into his character? Is scouting enabling him to

244
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,740
learn these important things in life? So this

245
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:40,380
makes the scout himself responsible for

246
00:15:40,380 --> 00:15:43,420
evaluating himself. It's a guided discussion.

247
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,820
We ask lots of questions, we go through it

248
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:48,380
and we let them make the final determination

249
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:50,140
whether or not they've completed that

250
00:15:50,140 --> 00:15:52,060
requirement. It kind of turns things a

251
00:15:52,060 --> 00:15:53,820
little bit on its head from what a lot of

252
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:56,060
us are used to doing. I would encourage you

253
00:15:56,060 --> 00:15:58,380
to give it a shot, see how well it works. I

254
00:15:58,380 --> 00:16:01,260
really depend on it. I think inviting the

255
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:03,260
scout's judgment into the question is a

256
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:05,420
very important thing for us to do. The

257
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:07,900
other aspect of these kind of judgment

258
00:16:07,900 --> 00:16:10,860
calls are two extremes that Peyton Powell

259
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:13,820
described. One is almost giving badges away

260
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:15,180
on a very slight knowledge of the

261
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,500
subjects. The other is to insist that

262
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,580
our scouts should be very first rate

263
00:16:19,580 --> 00:16:21,180
before they can get a requirement.

264
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:23,580
Between those two extremes, Peyton Powell

265
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:26,380
describes kind of a middle path, a right

266
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:29,260
way, and he says examiners using their

267
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:32,540
sense and discretion, keeping the main

268
00:16:32,540 --> 00:16:36,140
aim in view. Now, the main aim is put

269
00:16:36,140 --> 00:16:38,620
succinctly in the Guide to Advancement.

270
00:16:38,620 --> 00:16:40,540
I'm going to repeat it for a third time.

271
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,540
We know we're on the right track when

272
00:16:42,540 --> 00:16:45,580
we see youth accepting responsibility,

273
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:47,900
demonstrating self-reliance, caring for

274
00:16:47,900 --> 00:16:49,980
themselves and others, and when they

275
00:16:49,980 --> 00:16:51,900
learn to weave scouting ideals into

276
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:54,220
their lives, and when we see that they

277
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:56,060
will be positive contributors to

278
00:16:56,060 --> 00:16:58,140
American society And that's really

279
00:16:58,140 --> 00:17:00,939
everything right there. That is what we

280
00:17:00,939 --> 00:17:03,660
want to be looking for. That is the aim

281
00:17:03,660 --> 00:17:05,420
that we want to keep in view when we're

282
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:07,500
going through this testing part of

283
00:17:07,500 --> 00:17:09,819
advancement. Finally, we need to

284
00:17:09,819 --> 00:17:12,139
understand that none of us individually

285
00:17:12,139 --> 00:17:14,460
owns advancement. We don't own the

286
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:17,020
awards. I've never personally sat down

287
00:17:17,020 --> 00:17:18,700
and embroidered a Marriott badge patch

288
00:17:18,700 --> 00:17:20,859
for presentation. I've never personally

289
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:23,180
sat down and written out all the

290
00:17:23,180 --> 00:17:25,420
requirements for a Marriott badge.

291
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,420
We don't add or subtract from the

292
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:30,300
requirements. It's not our responsibility

293
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:33,420
to protect them from the unworthy.

294
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:36,860
What our responsibility is is to keep

295
00:17:36,860 --> 00:17:39,900
the main aim in view. If we go back

296
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,580
over the history of scouting, if we go

297
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:44,700
back and we start in 1910, if we go

298
00:17:44,700 --> 00:17:46,460
back to the earliest years of scouting,

299
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:48,060
we're going to find adults getting

300
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:49,660
frustrated with the quality of scout

301
00:17:49,660 --> 00:17:51,980
skills. It comes up again and again.

302
00:17:51,980 --> 00:17:54,620
It's nothing new. Getting frustrated is

303
00:17:54,620 --> 00:17:56,940
a pretty good indication that we may be

304
00:17:56,940 --> 00:17:59,020
missing the whole point of what we're

305
00:17:59,020 --> 00:18:02,620
doing, or the main aim, If a scout can't

306
00:18:02,620 --> 00:18:04,780
tie a square knot weeks or months after

307
00:18:04,780 --> 00:18:07,260
he was tested and approved as having

308
00:18:07,260 --> 00:18:09,420
attained that skill. some of us are

309
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:10,940
going to see it as a deficiency in

310
00:18:10,940 --> 00:18:13,260
instruction or a laxity of standards

311
00:18:13,260 --> 00:18:14,940
and really the impending end of any

312
00:18:14,940 --> 00:18:17,340
kind of integrity in scouting at all.

313
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:20,220
If our main aim was producing boys who

314
00:18:20,220 --> 00:18:22,620
could tie square knots on demand, I'd be

315
00:18:22,620 --> 00:18:24,060
worried about that.

316
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:26,300
Thankfully that's not our main aim.

317
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,899
Obviously we want the best for our

318
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:29,899
scouts. We really want them to learn

319
00:18:29,899 --> 00:18:32,620
things In some measure. their performance

320
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:34,780
is also a reflection of our own work,

321
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:35,659
right?

322
00:18:35,659 --> 00:18:38,060
So it's possible that a tinge of

323
00:18:38,060 --> 00:18:40,139
selfishness clouds our judgment when

324
00:18:40,139 --> 00:18:42,939
we get defensive and we try to protect

325
00:18:42,939 --> 00:18:45,340
advancement by insisting that scouts

326
00:18:45,340 --> 00:18:47,899
be first rate. As Baden Powell said,

327
00:18:47,899 --> 00:18:51,260
this is all very right in theory, in

328
00:18:51,260 --> 00:18:52,540
theory.

329
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:56,620
So if we get misdirected by this idea

330
00:18:56,620 --> 00:18:59,179
that high proficiency in scout skills

331
00:18:59,179 --> 00:19:01,899
are our aim, that's very right in

332
00:19:01,899 --> 00:19:02,780
theory.

333
00:19:02,780 --> 00:19:04,620
But what it does is it leads to some

334
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:06,379
very negative things happening. We

335
00:19:06,379 --> 00:19:08,459
start to crack down on the slackers

336
00:19:08,459 --> 00:19:10,220
and tighten things up and we get pretty

337
00:19:10,220 --> 00:19:11,260
intense

338
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:13,740
about making darn sure that we aren't

339
00:19:13,740 --> 00:19:15,500
giving any requirements away

340
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:17,420
And we get this kind of golem-like

341
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:19,900
preoccupation with the precious,

342
00:19:19,900 --> 00:19:22,860
this state of rigorous perfection, and

343
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:25,100
that diminishes the joy of scouting

344
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,220
for us

345
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:28,540
and for our scouts, and it's just

346
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:30,220
plain frustrating.

347
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:32,300
If we think about what Baden Powell

348
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:33,660
said and we dedicate ourselves to

349
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:35,820
keeping the main aim in view,

350
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:38,060
we learn that this kind of dogged

351
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:40,140
pursuit of perfection is having

352
00:19:40,140 --> 00:19:42,860
really an absolutely opposite effect of

353
00:19:42,860 --> 00:19:44,460
what we'd hoped it would produce, and

354
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:46,860
that is happy skilled scouts.

355
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:47,820
Okay,

356
00:19:47,820 --> 00:19:48,860
What we

357
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:51,020
end up doing is producing,

358
00:19:51,020 --> 00:19:53,260
perhaps, scouts who can tie square knots

359
00:19:53,260 --> 00:19:54,380
on demand,

360
00:19:54,380 --> 00:19:56,860
but they are deriving from the program

361
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:58,060
what the program

362
00:19:58,060 --> 00:19:59,420
is aimed at.

363
00:19:59,420 --> 00:20:01,500
F Darnell Daly Jr

364
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:04,460
is the Advancement Chair for Area 6

365
00:20:04,460 --> 00:20:06,140
of the Northeast Region

366
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:07,980
and he wrote something that has been

367
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:09,820
circulating around for quite a while

368
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:11,580
now and many of you may be familiar

369
00:20:11,580 --> 00:20:12,300
with it,

370
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,980
and it's a. it's a little writing called

371
00:20:13,980 --> 00:20:15,500
Guardians at the Gate

372
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:17,100
and I want to read a little bit of it

373
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,260
to close out this installment.

374
00:20:19,260 --> 00:20:21,180
He says: some of you appear to be

375
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:23,260
standing guard at the gate.

376
00:20:23,260 --> 00:20:25,419
like good guards, you are not letting

377
00:20:25,419 --> 00:20:26,540
anyone pass

378
00:20:26,540 --> 00:20:28,860
who does not have the correct

379
00:20:28,860 --> 00:20:30,379
password.

380
00:20:30,379 --> 00:20:31,980
When someone appears at the gate who

381
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,659
does not have the correct password, you

382
00:20:33,659 --> 00:20:35,020
send them away.

383
00:20:35,020 --> 00:20:37,020
The treasure that you believe you are

384
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:38,780
guarding is the sacred

385
00:20:38,780 --> 00:20:41,180
advancement requirements.

386
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,780
You believe that you must guard the

387
00:20:42,780 --> 00:20:44,540
gate to make sure that no boy

388
00:20:44,540 --> 00:20:45,820
advances

389
00:20:45,820 --> 00:20:48,380
who has not only met the requirements

390
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:51,500
but who has met the requirements 110

391
00:20:51,500 --> 00:20:52,140
percent.

392
00:20:52,140 --> 00:20:53,580
Your watchword is:

393
00:20:53,580 --> 00:20:55,420
we've gotten soft on Boy Scout

394
00:20:55,420 --> 00:20:56,940
Advancement.

395
00:20:56,940 --> 00:20:59,100
The problem is that you've got your

396
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:00,140
orders wrong.

397
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:01,660
you're guarding the wrong side of the

398
00:21:01,660 --> 00:21:02,300
gate.

399
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:05,420
The treasure is not behind the gate

400
00:21:05,420 --> 00:21:07,340
but in front of it.

401
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:09,660
The treasure is the character of the

402
00:21:09,660 --> 00:21:11,820
boys in our care.

403
00:21:11,820 --> 00:21:14,540
Your duty is not to prevent boys from

404
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:16,380
passing through

405
00:21:16,380 --> 00:21:18,940
but to make sure as many boys as

406
00:21:18,940 --> 00:21:19,820
possible

407
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,260
do pass through.

408
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:22,540
I'll have a link in the post that

409
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,700
contains this podcast to that complete

410
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,580
quote.

411
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:27,020
It creates a picture that I think

412
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:29,260
really helps drive this home.

413
00:21:29,260 --> 00:21:31,740
So a scout is tested.

414
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:33,660
a scout gets tested once.

415
00:21:33,660 --> 00:21:35,500
He can challenge a requirement as many

416
00:21:35,500 --> 00:21:37,100
times as necessary.

417
00:21:37,100 --> 00:21:38,780
Some requirements are certified

418
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:41,180
through a simple check off process,

419
00:21:41,180 --> 00:21:43,340
Some require some judgment.

420
00:21:43,340 --> 00:21:45,260
If we invite the scouts

421
00:21:45,260 --> 00:21:48,060
personal judgment into the question,

422
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:50,460
it will help both them and us.

423
00:21:50,460 --> 00:21:51,740
And finally,

424
00:21:51,740 --> 00:21:52,860
we don't want

425
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:54,780
to follow either extreme

426
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:56,780
of just giving stuff away

427
00:21:56,780 --> 00:21:57,660
or

428
00:21:57,660 --> 00:21:58,940
guarding the gate.

429
00:21:58,940 --> 00:22:00,780
We want that middle road

430
00:22:00,780 --> 00:22:03,820
where as many boys as possible do pass

431
00:22:03,820 --> 00:22:04,940
through that gate,

432
00:22:04,940 --> 00:22:06,379
And we do this

433
00:22:06,379 --> 00:22:07,420
by keeping

434
00:22:07,420 --> 00:22:08,940
the main aim

435
00:22:08,940 --> 00:22:09,900
in view.

436
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,340
So in the next podcast we're going to

437
00:22:11,340 --> 00:22:13,260
talk about step number three

438
00:22:13,260 --> 00:22:14,780
in scout advancement,

439
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:17,180
that is, a scout is reviewed.

